            {
                "entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
                "word": "hébétude",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ccd432c9-686a-437d-9940-d70c869b1841",
                        "entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hébétudes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0ea3bc5-daeb-3944-af2f-e6a84c7518ee",
                        "entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Engourdissement des facultés cérébrales dans certaines maladies, l’anémie cérébrale, par exemple."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                        "entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Apparence ou comportement d’une personne qui semble soudain engourdie ou sidérée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20bd804d-fbae-40e4-8fc7-ef4532a5b25f",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "La soudaineté chirurgicale de leur rupture le laissa stupide. Seul dans cette maison que leur couple, quasi conjugal, habitait depuis quelque vingt ans, il ne parvenait pas, au bout de huit jours, à s’évader de l’hébétude pour entrer dans le chagrin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca54eaaf-6156-4e4a-8297-5d5cc3124a4d",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "Un monsieur, courant, une serviette sous le bras, le heurta sans ménagements et l’arracha à son hébétude."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c15547a-4944-43e8-a55e-6d9033559159",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "Il se tut et retomba dans son hébétude."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86705cdd-5200-472e-964a-e4e8d0b87dab",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "Il la pénétrait bestialement, dans une hébétude sensuelle qui n'atteignait à la lucidité qu'à la minute où l'on voit, par une nuit d'été, la fusée d'un feu d'artifice fondre en un riche bouquet d'étoiles pâmées qui retombent au néant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09b2bde1-cb7a-4eba-8457-cce70a26feaf",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "Cette considération le plongea dans une sorte d’hébétude douloureuse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6c8a6b4-d51b-4897-8a39-0961b0ea4ff1",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "De sa bouche lisse, Amédée souriait, repris par l’hébétude de l’enfance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24dd71ff-b9c5-4a8c-864d-9ef0344ed825",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "À présent, une émission télévisée fera l’affaire. La plus idiote conviendra. Ah – regarder pour regarder, sans alibi, sans désir, sans excuse ! C’est comme l’eau du bain : une hébétude qui vous engourdit d’un bien-être palpable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d3cb753-563e-4af2-9d41-4562a80dc79c",
                                "sense_id": "adc3eb99-7e9c-36f4-9798-a568539c8285",
                                "text": "Pour une fois que j’ai l’occasion de parler de cette histoire… Elle a pourtant quelque chose d’une vieille putain réduite à l’hébétude par l’excès des hommes, cette histoire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84a6ce93-30da-481c-95bc-7181fbc122d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
                        "target_lang_word": "hebetude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hebetude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                        "entry_id": "1e9be929-66c6-39f2-a2e4-b96f5b89c9d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mental lethargy or dullness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a0cf127-9ecb-450f-b30d-5244e65a9c6f",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "1600, translation attributed to Thomas Nashe, The Hospitall of Incurable Fooles by Tomaso Garzoni, London: Edward Blount, Discourse 6, pp. 32-33,\nThe intemperature of the braine is the cause of al this (as phisitions affirme) which maketh all the officiall, and functiue parts full of heauines and indisposition, and so through this hebetude (to vse their terme) vnapt to keepe in minde any thing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82e7a080-cb0d-4445-87f4-5e0d75fe7b65",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "[T]here are ſeveral Species of Writing, in which a proper Degree of Hebetude is abſolutely neceſſary, as well as in other profeſſions; such as Lexicography, Index-making, and the like; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b155893-99f6-4baf-806a-1e687ca309f8",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "It would be a supposition attended with very little probability, to believe that a complete and full formed spirit existed in every infant; but that it was clogged and impeded in its operations, during the first twenty years of life, by the weakness, or hebetude, of the organs in which it was enclosed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d50c0bf7-ef51-4bd6-97b1-e2183e8e89ae",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "Hirsch, with his arms tied behind his back, had been bundled violently into one of the smaller rooms. For many hours he remained apparently forgotten, stretched lifelessly on the floor. From that solitude, full of despair and terror, he was torn out brutally, with kicks and blows, passive, sunk in hebetude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0adf6a61-87e5-494b-86cb-100fd0fa039f",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "Incuriousness was the most potent ally of our imposed order; for Eastern government rested not so much on consent or force, as on the common supinity, hebetude, lack-a-daisiness, which gave a minority undue effect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef980407-c795-4180-b6e8-df7c49fd958e",
                                                "sense_id": "6371d760-aece-3e00-a7f7-b5e1e54abc5a",
                                                "text": "1985, Oliver Sacks, “The Lost Mariner”, chapter 2 in The Man Who Mistook His Wife for a Hat (Reset 2007 edition), page 33, footnote 2,\nThis dwelling on the past and relative hebetude towards the present – this emotional dulling of current feeling and memory – is nothing like Jimmie’s organic amnesia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a291df2-853e-4e37-9135-9d164efea0c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac6d8cdd-41b7-3071-bbff-f79791b6c1d9",
